To correctly close a Dyck-n word, we need to match each opening parenthesis with a corresponding closing parenthesis of the same type. 

Q: Complete the rest of the sequence, making sure that the parentheses are closed properly. Input: < > ( ( [ [ ( { } ) [ < > ] ]
A: ] ) ) 

Explanation: The input has 6 opening parentheses and 6 corresponding closing parentheses. The correct sequence is: < > ( ( [ [ ( { } ) [ < > ] ] ) ] ) 

Q: Complete the rest of the sequence, making sure that the parentheses are closed properly. Input: < [ < [ { < [ ] < { } > > } ] > { { ( ) } { < [ < > ] > }
A: } ] > 

Explanation: The input has 7 opening parentheses and 7 corresponding closing parentheses. The correct sequence is: < [ < [ { < [ ] < { } > > } ] > { { ( ) } { < [ < > ] > } ] > } 

Q: Complete the rest of the sequence, making sure that the parentheses are closed properly. Input: < < { ( < ( ) > ) }
A: > ) } > 

Explanation: The input has 4 opening parentheses and 4 corresponding closing parentheses. The correct sequence is: < < { ( < ( ) > ) > ) } >
